<title>SPAIN: Spain metals association sees H2 activity pick-up.</title>
<headline>Spain metals association sees H2 activity pick-up.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish metal firms are expecting a pick-up in activity in the second half of the year, according to the July survey from Confemetal metal firms' association.</p>
<p>In the first quarter, production of steel fell 4.5 percent. Imports rose 4.9 percent and exports fell 4.8 percent. Apparent consumption rose 4.7 percent, Confemetal said.</p>
<p>During the same period, copper consumption was little changed, and production for export increased. Copper output rose 9.6 percent, with imports down 2.6 percent and exports up 27.7 percent.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
